1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,134
["Flower Ring" by Shino Shimoji
and Aya Suzaki plays]

2
00:01:32,397 --> 00:01:35,574
[footsteps approaching]

3
00:01:35,704 --> 00:01:38,620
- Now then, time to get
today's work started.

4
00:01:38,751 --> 00:01:40,144
Hmm?

5
00:01:41,797 --> 00:01:43,625
What, Zabuton?

6
00:01:44,409 --> 00:01:45,671
Hmm?

7
00:01:46,473 --> 00:01:47,431
A bee?

8
00:01:47,571 --> 00:01:49,094
It's huge.

9
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:50,850
What will you do with it?

10
00:01:50,997 --> 00:01:53,521
Are you going to eat it?

11
00:01:53,676 --> 00:01:56,287
So then you'll keep it as a pet?

12
00:01:57,759 --> 00:02:00,458
Yeah, it might be dangerous.

13
00:02:00,613 --> 00:02:03,181
Oh, it won't fight back anymore?

14
00:02:03,335 --> 00:02:05,032
Okay, got it.

15
00:02:08,997 --> 00:02:10,651
There we go.

16
00:02:10,796 --> 00:02:14,147
I built a little house for the
bee's nest near the orchard.

17
00:02:14,308 --> 00:02:17,790
They built a big nest inside
in about 10 days.

18
00:02:17,949 --> 00:02:20,865
The worker bees are all busy
taking care of their jobs.

19
00:02:21,021 --> 00:02:24,328
By the way, only the queen
is that big.

20
00:02:24,487 --> 00:02:26,750
The worker bees are all
normal-sized.

21
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:28,597
If I leave them here like this,

22
00:02:28,742 --> 00:02:30,918
I wonder if they'll make honey
that I can harvest.

23
00:02:31,066 --> 00:02:33,721
The crops in the field
have flowering plants,

24
00:02:33,874 --> 00:02:36,180
but maybe I should plant
a flower garden nearby

25
00:02:36,329 --> 00:02:37,809
if I wanna harvest honey.

26
00:02:37,951 --> 00:02:38,909
- Hello?

27
00:02:39,048 --> 00:02:40,136
Hiraku?

28
00:02:40,276 --> 00:02:41,407
[Tia screaming]

29
00:02:41,547 --> 00:02:43,636
Pardon the intrusion!

30
00:02:43,784 --> 00:02:47,657
- Maybe she's been stung
before or something.

31
00:02:47,817 --> 00:02:50,950
[hammer tapping]

32
00:02:51,105 --> 00:02:52,759
[Hiraku grunting]

33
00:02:55,005 --> 00:02:56,311
[Hiraku sighing]

34
00:02:56,451 --> 00:02:57,365
- What's this?

35
00:02:57,503 --> 00:02:58,896
- Reservoir.

36
00:02:59,037 --> 00:03:00,909
Or at least it will be one day.

37
00:03:01,053 --> 00:03:02,228
I planned on drawing water

38
00:03:02,368 --> 00:03:04,152
from the river
through a waterway,

39
00:03:04,296 --> 00:03:06,559
and I've been busy with
other stuff lately.

40
00:03:06,705 --> 00:03:08,142
- I see, then.

41
00:03:08,282 --> 00:03:09,762
How far have you progressed

42
00:03:09,904 --> 00:03:11,470
with the waterway construction?

43
00:03:11,612 --> 00:03:12,918
- Not even far enough to decide

44
00:03:13,058 --> 00:03:15,278
what I'm going to
make out of it yet.

45
00:03:15,423 --> 00:03:17,556
There's actually
quite a bit of distance

46
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:19,311
between here and the river.

47
00:03:19,452 --> 00:03:21,715
- [Lea] First we need to decide
what to build it out of.

48
00:03:21,861 --> 00:03:23,297
- [Hiraku] Let's see.

49
00:03:23,438 --> 00:03:26,180
I've always pictured waterways
as built from stone.

50
00:03:26,328 --> 00:03:27,808
- [Lea] Hm.

51
00:03:27,948 --> 00:03:29,820
I think it would be a bit
difficult to find stone

52
00:03:29,962 --> 00:03:31,442
to work with around here.

53
00:03:31,583 --> 00:03:33,802
- Then should we use wood?

54
00:03:33,946 --> 00:03:36,818
- Well, we certainly do have
a lot of wood here,

55
00:03:36,967 --> 00:03:38,490
but if we have a long waterway,

56
00:03:38,631 --> 00:03:40,720
the gaps in the wood will
cause quite a bit of leakage.

57
00:03:40,863 --> 00:03:42,561
- Hm.
[water dripping]

58
00:03:42,701 --> 00:03:45,008
In that case, we'll use this.

59
00:03:45,153 --> 00:03:48,417
[hammer thumping]

60
00:03:48,566 --> 00:03:51,700
A compacted dirt,
using the almighty tool.

61
00:03:51,847 --> 00:03:53,545
It's about as hard as concrete.

62
00:03:53,685 --> 00:03:54,599
This should work great.

63
00:03:54,736 --> 00:03:56,041
- As what?

64
00:03:56,179 --> 00:03:57,702
- Oh, never mind.

65
00:03:57,842 --> 00:03:59,800
I actually had a mountain
of dirt left over

66
00:03:59,942 --> 00:04:01,204
from digging out the reservoir

67
00:04:01,342 --> 00:04:02,952
that I wasn't sure
what to do with.

68
00:04:03,091 --> 00:04:05,093
We went right into
mass production mode.

69
00:04:05,235 --> 00:04:07,150
- [All] One! Two! One!

70
00:04:07,291 --> 00:04:08,422
- [Hiraku] Next!

71
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:10,213
We built an intake gate
for the water

72
00:04:10,353 --> 00:04:11,746
at the top of the waterfall,

73
00:04:11,883 --> 00:04:14,277
then built up the
foundation using dirt,

74
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:16,857
and placed parts of the
waterway on top of it.

75
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,655
- [Lea] Okay. A little
more this way.

76
00:04:19,799 --> 00:04:21,409
[Lea grunting]

77
00:04:21,548 --> 00:04:22,723
[Leezay humming]

78
00:04:22,859 --> 00:04:23,947
- [Hiraku] I let
the elves handle

79
00:04:24,083 --> 00:04:25,214
the basic foundation work.

80
00:04:25,351 --> 00:04:27,658
- Good work.
- Good work!

81
00:04:27,799 --> 00:04:30,062
- [Hiraku] I focused on
sealing the seams

82
00:04:30,204 --> 00:04:32,424
and strengthening
the foundation.

83
00:04:32,564 --> 00:04:34,174
Thanks to all of
their hard work,

84
00:04:34,313 --> 00:04:35,445
the construction moved along

85
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:37,930
a lot faster than
I was expecting.

86
00:04:38,072 --> 00:04:39,508
[water rushing]

87
00:04:39,645 --> 00:04:41,342
[water splashing]

88
00:04:42,835 --> 00:04:44,793
[Lea laughing]

89
00:04:44,933 --> 00:04:46,978
Now we won't have to climb
in and out of the well

90
00:04:47,118 --> 00:04:48,728
for water every day.

91
00:04:48,865 --> 00:04:50,214
- Yeah!

92
00:04:50,350 --> 00:04:52,265
This should make watering
the crops easier, too.

93
00:04:53,322 --> 00:04:54,149
[fish flapping]

94
00:04:54,282 --> 00:04:55,893
- Oh, look at this.

95
00:04:56,030 --> 00:04:57,684
I haven't been able
to catch any,

96
00:04:57,822 --> 00:04:59,432
but now that we have
access to the river,

97
00:04:59,569 --> 00:05:01,396
I can finally eat fish.

98
00:05:01,534 --> 00:05:04,102
I just need to decide how
I'm going to prepare them.

99
00:05:04,242 --> 00:05:07,289
You know, the rabbits in this
forest may be really vicious,

100
00:05:07,430 --> 00:05:09,955
but the fish here seem
to be pretty normal.

101
00:05:10,094 --> 00:05:11,661
I'm really glad that
they're so easy to-

102
00:05:11,798 --> 00:05:13,190
[fish thudding]
[Hiraku screaming]

103
00:05:13,326 --> 00:05:14,588
[blade ringing]

104
00:05:14,724 --> 00:05:15,855
- Oh!

105
00:05:15,990 --> 00:05:17,687
[wood rattling]
[fire crackling]

106
00:05:17,824 --> 00:05:22,263
- [Lu] Aren't those fish from
the forest of death waters?

107
00:05:22,408 --> 00:05:23,583
- Yeah.

108
00:05:23,718 --> 00:05:25,154
Those are the really
vicious ones, too.

109
00:05:25,290 --> 00:05:27,031
- I wonder if it's
safe to eat those.

110
00:05:27,167 --> 00:05:28,691
[all humming]

111
00:05:28,826 --> 00:05:31,350
[triumphant chord playing]

112
00:05:32,318 --> 00:05:33,014
- Here you go.

113
00:05:33,147 --> 00:05:33,887
Just for you.

114
00:05:34,020 --> 00:05:35,108
- Oh no. [laughing]

115
00:05:35,242 --> 00:05:35,895
You should eat first.

116
00:05:36,028 --> 00:05:36,812
You made it.

117
00:05:36,944 --> 00:05:37,815
- Yeah, she's right.

118
00:05:37,948 --> 00:05:39,645
You're the one who made it.

119
00:05:39,781 --> 00:05:41,217
- Are you sure?

120
00:05:41,352 --> 00:05:42,875
Then I'll help myself.

121
00:05:43,011 --> 00:05:44,752
[relaxed music playing]

122
00:05:44,887 --> 00:05:47,760
[Hiraku chewing]

123
00:05:47,898 --> 00:05:50,074
It looks and tastes
just like salmon!

124
00:05:50,211 --> 00:05:51,342
- Like ham?

125
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:52,912
- [Hiraku] Uh, forget
what I said.

126
00:05:53,047 --> 00:05:54,744
Here, don't be shy.
[both gasping]

127
00:05:54,879 --> 00:05:56,924
Eat up.

128
00:05:57,060 --> 00:05:59,323
[both whimpering]

129
00:06:03,342 --> 00:06:04,909
[Lu gulping]

130
00:06:05,043 --> 00:06:06,262
- This is...

131
00:06:06,395 --> 00:06:07,092
- So...

132
00:06:07,223 --> 00:06:08,790
So delicious!

133
00:06:09,710 --> 00:06:11,059
[all murmuring]

134
00:06:11,193 --> 00:06:14,370
- So would you all
like to try some?

135
00:06:14,507 --> 00:06:15,726
- [All] Mhm!

136
00:06:15,859 --> 00:06:17,208
- [Hiraku] They all loved it,

137
00:06:17,341 --> 00:06:19,082
so we quickly
went through it all.

138
00:06:19,217 --> 00:06:20,653
But after that, we caught more

139
00:06:20,786 --> 00:06:23,311
and preserved it with salt
so we could store them.

140
00:06:24,536 --> 00:06:26,103
[relaxed music ending]

141
00:06:26,237 --> 00:06:28,195
I decided to try
tilling with the hoe

142
00:06:28,330 --> 00:06:30,114
while thinking about
rice plants,

143
00:06:30,248 --> 00:06:32,032
and rice plants popped up.

144
00:06:32,166 --> 00:06:34,777
I didn't know that they
could grow in normal soil

145
00:06:34,913 --> 00:06:37,437
but now that we have the
waterways built here...

146
00:06:37,571 --> 00:06:38,529
[drum banging]

147
00:06:38,661 --> 00:06:39,967
We're building a rice paddy.

148
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:42,885
- Did you say a paddy?

149
00:06:43,020 --> 00:06:44,891
[hoe swiping]
[Hiraku grunting]

150
00:06:45,025 --> 00:06:46,896
[grand music beginning]

151
00:06:48,685 --> 00:06:50,774
[Hiraku grunting]

152
00:06:52,085 --> 00:06:53,652
[elves humming]

153
00:06:59,144 --> 00:07:00,493
- Huh?

154
00:07:00,625 --> 00:07:02,671
- It looks just like a
normal crop field, though.

155
00:07:02,803 --> 00:07:04,849
- [Hiraku] I'm just
getting started here.

156
00:07:04,983 --> 00:07:06,854
[wood rattling]
[water rushing]

157
00:07:07,989 --> 00:07:09,468
[elves gasping]
- Oh!

158
00:07:15,438 --> 00:07:17,614
- [Lea] Are you building
a pond too?

159
00:07:17,746 --> 00:07:19,270
Oh, I know what it's!

160
00:07:19,401 --> 00:07:21,099
You're going to keep
fish here, right?

161
00:07:21,230 --> 00:07:23,667
- [laughing] I guess
that's how it looks.

162
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:25,845
Now, I'm going to need
you all to help me

163
00:07:25,978 --> 00:07:27,023
with this next part.

164
00:07:27,154 --> 00:07:29,243
- What? What should we do?

165
00:07:30,768 --> 00:07:32,640
[water splashing]

166
00:07:32,771 --> 00:07:34,904
It's all slimy.

167
00:07:35,036 --> 00:07:36,907
[Lea whining]

168
00:07:37,039 --> 00:07:39,693
[elves murmuring]

169
00:07:39,826 --> 00:07:43,569
- Okay, everyone, let's plant
all these seedlings.

170
00:07:46,182 --> 00:07:47,575
- Ah!

171
00:07:48,968 --> 00:07:50,144
[Lees grunting]

172
00:07:50,274 --> 00:07:51,841
[Leef and Leely laughing]

173
00:07:55,455 --> 00:07:57,370
The girls were a little
nervous at first,

174
00:07:57,501 --> 00:07:58,980
but they got the hang of it.

175
00:08:00,243 --> 00:08:02,114
The rice planting went off
without a hitch.

176
00:08:02,246 --> 00:08:04,509
I put Zabuton's children
in charge

177
00:08:04,639 --> 00:08:06,163
of keeping pests
out of the area.

178
00:08:06,293 --> 00:08:08,861
I'm not sure if it was
thanks to the water

179
00:08:08,991 --> 00:08:10,558
or the almighty farming tool,

180
00:08:10,689 --> 00:08:11,907
[elves cheering]

181
00:08:12,038 --> 00:08:13,779
but the rice plants
grew much faster

182
00:08:13,909 --> 00:08:15,520
than I expected them to.

183
00:08:16,608 --> 00:08:18,479
And now, it's time to harvest.

184
00:08:18,609 --> 00:08:21,612
I had Lea and the girls
help me with this too,

185
00:08:21,742 --> 00:08:23,657
[blades ringing]
[elves grunting]

186
00:08:23,787 --> 00:08:26,920
and thanks to them, it was done
in the blink of an eye.

187
00:08:27,051 --> 00:08:28,879
[relaxed music]

188
00:08:30,879 --> 00:08:33,708
- [Lea] So what exactly
are we doing?

189
00:08:33,837 --> 00:08:36,405
- We're drying them so we can
get all the moisture out.

190
00:08:36,535 --> 00:08:38,189
- Huh?

191
00:08:38,319 --> 00:08:41,148
You know about all kinds of
interesting things, don't you?

192
00:08:41,277 --> 00:08:43,583
- [laughs] I just
happened upon this.

193
00:08:43,713 --> 00:08:45,367
That's right.

194
00:08:45,496 --> 00:08:48,891
I just happened to watch an idol
doing this on TV one time.

195
00:08:49,803 --> 00:08:51,457
- [Lu] Hmm.

196
00:08:51,586 --> 00:08:54,328
So these are the crops
you grew in that paddy, then?

197
00:08:54,457 --> 00:08:56,676
- What are you going
to do with them now?

198
00:08:56,806 --> 00:08:58,068
- We'll thresh them.

199
00:08:58,198 --> 00:08:59,112
- You'll thresh them?

200
00:08:59,241 --> 00:09:00,199
- Yep.
- Ah.

201
00:09:00,328 --> 00:09:01,938
- Let's see...

202
00:09:03,634 --> 00:09:06,289
I'm pretty sure the old
thresher I saw in a museum

203
00:09:06,417 --> 00:09:08,158
looks something like this.

204
00:09:08,287 --> 00:09:10,376
[Hiraku grunting]
[plants rustling]

205
00:09:10,504 --> 00:09:11,810
[girls applauding]

206
00:09:11,939 --> 00:09:14,159
[laughing] That's
the gist of it.

207
00:09:14,288 --> 00:09:15,637
[rice shuffling]

208
00:09:15,766 --> 00:09:17,246
Next, we put them
through a sieve

209
00:09:17,375 --> 00:09:19,464
to get rid of any remaining
leaves or plant matter.

210
00:09:19,592 --> 00:09:20,680
- Oh.
- Oh!

211
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:21,854
- [Hiraku] Then we
use a mortar

212
00:09:21,984 --> 00:09:23,290
to remove the husk
from the rice,

213
00:09:23,419 --> 00:09:25,682
and now we use a pestle
to polish the rice.

214
00:09:25,810 --> 00:09:27,986
[Lecott sighing]
[pestle thumping]

215
00:09:28,115 --> 00:09:30,508
- This stuff really
takes a lot of work.

216
00:09:30,636 --> 00:09:31,550
- Yeah.

217
00:09:31,679 --> 00:09:32,985
Can you not eat it

218
00:09:33,114 --> 00:09:34,941
if you don't go through
all these steps?

219
00:09:35,070 --> 00:09:37,203
[rice glittering]

220
00:09:37,331 --> 00:09:38,419
[Hiraku sighing]

221
00:09:38,548 --> 00:09:40,854
- Are you finally finished?
- Yeah.

222
00:09:40,982 --> 00:09:43,550
- So that means we can
eat it now, doesn't it?

223
00:09:43,677 --> 00:09:45,114
- No, not yet.

224
00:09:45,242 --> 00:09:46,548
[Lu groaning]
[Tia gasping]

225
00:09:46,677 --> 00:09:48,114
[gentle music playing]

226
00:09:48,242 --> 00:09:49,809
- What happens now?

227
00:09:49,937 --> 00:09:51,678
- I'm cooking the rice.

228
00:09:51,806 --> 00:09:54,983
If I remember the way to
cook rice in a kettle

229
00:09:55,110 --> 00:09:58,852
first you start it nice and
slow, and then once it rises

230
00:09:58,978 --> 00:10:00,632
cut the heat and simmer,

231
00:10:00,759 --> 00:10:02,718
add a fist full of straw
to the fire.

232
00:10:02,845 --> 00:10:05,718
Then no matter what happens,
don't lift the lid.

233
00:10:05,844 --> 00:10:07,107
- Was that a spell?

234
00:10:07,235 --> 00:10:08,236
- Don't know.

235
00:10:08,365 --> 00:10:09,975
I've never heard it before.

236
00:10:10,104 --> 00:10:11,279
- [Hiraku] Hey, Lu?

237
00:10:11,407 --> 00:10:13,017
- Hmm?
- Huh?

238
00:10:13,145 --> 00:10:14,755
- [Hiraku] Could you use
your magic to light the fire?

239
00:10:14,884 --> 00:10:16,320
- [Lu] Sure, I'd be happy to.

240
00:10:16,448 --> 00:10:18,145
It's finally time
for the great sage

241
00:10:18,274 --> 00:10:20,841
Lord Lulucy to show
what she can do.

242
00:10:20,967 --> 00:10:23,970
I'll blast you one and all
into smithereens!

243
00:10:24,097 --> 00:10:27,709
- Uh... It's supposed to be
slow, so a low flame.

244
00:10:27,833 --> 00:10:28,834
- Aw, come on.

245
00:10:28,963 --> 00:10:30,443
How incredibly boring.

246
00:10:30,570 --> 00:10:31,963
[fire roaring]

247
00:10:32,092 --> 00:10:33,702
I wonder what kind of food
he's making this time.

248
00:10:33,829 --> 00:10:35,309
- [Tia] I'm not sure
what he's making,

249
00:10:35,437 --> 00:10:37,569
but I'm curious to see
what the spell did.

250
00:10:37,696 --> 00:10:39,001
[Lecott gulping]

251
00:10:39,130 --> 00:10:41,089
[lid rattling]
[chimes tinkling]

252
00:10:41,215 --> 00:10:42,260
- [Hiraku] Oh!

253
00:10:42,388 --> 00:10:43,868
It came out perfect.

254
00:10:43,995 --> 00:10:45,214
- It's done now, right?

255
00:10:45,343 --> 00:10:46,387
- Not yet.

256
00:10:46,516 --> 00:10:47,778
[Lu grunting]

257
00:10:47,905 --> 00:10:49,516
- [All] Oh!

258
00:10:49,643 --> 00:10:52,124
[Hiraku grunting]

259
00:10:52,251 --> 00:10:56,298
[rice sparkling]

260
00:10:56,421 --> 00:10:59,554
- This thing here is what he
spent all that time making?

261
00:10:59,679 --> 00:11:00,767
- [Hiraku] Yeah.

262
00:11:00,895 --> 00:11:02,245
If you're going to try rice,

263
00:11:02,372 --> 00:11:04,853
then I think rice balls
are the way to go.

264
00:11:04,978 --> 00:11:06,545
- Well, after you then.

265
00:11:06,673 --> 00:11:07,761
[Lu gasping]

266
00:11:07,889 --> 00:11:09,543
- Fine, I'll do it.

267
00:11:09,670 --> 00:11:10,671
[Lu inhaling]

268
00:11:10,799 --> 00:11:12,845
[Lu chewing]

269
00:11:13,406 --> 00:11:14,798
Mm!

270
00:11:14,926 --> 00:11:15,927
Mhm!
[whimsical music playing]

271
00:11:16,056 --> 00:11:17,057
- Ah?

272
00:11:17,749 --> 00:11:19,359
[Tia chewing]

273
00:11:19,487 --> 00:11:20,836
Mm!

274
00:11:20,963 --> 00:11:22,530
It's delicious.

275
00:11:22,658 --> 00:11:23,833
- Glad to hear.

276
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:25,179
- Wait a sec.

277
00:11:25,307 --> 00:11:27,135
This is the fish
from the other day!

278
00:11:27,261 --> 00:11:29,481
- [Hiraku] Yeah, the saltiness
goes with the rice.

279
00:11:29,607 --> 00:11:31,087
- Mm.

280
00:11:31,214 --> 00:11:33,955
Now I feel like all that
hard work was worth it.

281
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:35,734
- Mhm.

282
00:11:35,861 --> 00:11:38,734
This is my happiest moment
as a farmer here yet.

283
00:11:38,858 --> 00:11:40,251
Huh?

284
00:11:44,027 --> 00:11:44,897
Are they good?

285
00:11:45,026 --> 00:11:46,201
- [All] Mhm!

286
00:11:46,328 --> 00:11:48,243
- Well, it looks
like they're a hit.

287
00:11:48,370 --> 00:11:50,807
I'll just have to work
harder and make more.

288
00:11:50,931 --> 00:11:52,237
[Hiraku chewing]

289
00:11:52,365 --> 00:11:54,715
Next time, I think I'll do
a different filling.

290
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:57,669
[delicate music playing]

291
00:11:58,835 --> 00:12:01,186
[leaves rustling]
[water sloshing]

292
00:12:01,311 --> 00:12:02,443
[Hiraku sighing]

293
00:12:02,570 --> 00:12:04,442
We should stop here for today.

294
00:12:04,567 --> 00:12:05,829
- Okay.

295
00:12:05,957 --> 00:12:09,265
[rustic music beginning]

296
00:12:09,388 --> 00:12:10,999
[light ringing]
[Lea humming]

297
00:12:12,862 --> 00:12:15,778
[light ringing]
[Leely grunting]

298
00:12:15,901 --> 00:12:18,252
[light ringing]
[Leef and Leezay humming]

299
00:12:19,289 --> 00:12:20,899
[water splashing]

300
00:12:21,026 --> 00:12:21,984
[light ringing]
[Lees and Leeta giggling]

301
00:12:22,111 --> 00:12:23,591
[both gasping]

302
00:12:25,108 --> 00:12:26,805
[Lecott groaning]

303
00:12:26,932 --> 00:12:28,455
[Lecott sneezing]
[light ringing]

304
00:12:28,582 --> 00:12:29,887
[Lecott sniffling]

305
00:12:31,665 --> 00:12:34,885
- Apparently they can all clean
themselves off with magic.

306
00:12:35,008 --> 00:12:36,749
It's times like this
I really wish

307
00:12:36,875 --> 00:12:38,790
I had a bath I could hop in.

308
00:12:38,916 --> 00:12:43,007
Well, I did build a waterway,
so I'll give it a shot.

309
00:12:46,341 --> 00:12:48,691
- You're building a bath?

310
00:12:48,817 --> 00:12:49,774
- Yeah.

311
00:12:49,902 --> 00:12:51,686
- What's a bath, exactly?

312
00:12:51,813 --> 00:12:55,556
- It's a place where you wash
your body with warm water.

313
00:12:55,677 --> 00:12:57,592
A furnace to heat up the water,

314
00:12:57,718 --> 00:12:59,459
a tub to hold the water,

315
00:12:59,585 --> 00:13:01,544
a place to wash your body.

316
00:13:01,669 --> 00:13:03,802
I wanna put a changing room
in there too.

317
00:13:03,928 --> 00:13:05,190
- Huh?

318
00:13:05,316 --> 00:13:06,665
- [Lea] Can't we just
wash ourselves

319
00:13:06,793 --> 00:13:08,186
in a river or something?

320
00:13:08,313 --> 00:13:10,402
- [Hiraku] Isn't it too cold
during the winter?

321
00:13:10,527 --> 00:13:12,224
- [Lea] Yeah, I guess
you're right.

322
00:13:12,351 --> 00:13:13,091
- Just trust me!

323
00:13:13,219 --> 00:13:14,481
Baths are great!

324
00:13:14,609 --> 00:13:16,611
I want to build one,
no matter what it takes.

325
00:13:16,736 --> 00:13:17,955
It's good for your circulation.

326
00:13:18,083 --> 00:13:19,432
- [Lea] We'll help you build it.

327
00:13:19,558 --> 00:13:21,038
[bright music playing]

328
00:13:21,166 --> 00:13:23,429
- [Hiraku] And so construction
began right away.

329
00:13:23,553 --> 00:13:25,294
The furnace was made
from blocks of dirt

330
00:13:25,421 --> 00:13:26,465
compacted with the hammer.

331
00:13:26,593 --> 00:13:28,290
- Oh!
- Oh!

332
00:13:28,417 --> 00:13:29,679
- [Hiraku] We fed it water
brought in from the waterway,

333
00:13:29,806 --> 00:13:32,070
and the most important
part of the bath,

334
00:13:32,194 --> 00:13:33,500
the tub itself.
[Lea giggling]

335
00:13:33,627 --> 00:13:36,152
I wanna make it
as big as possible.

336
00:13:36,276 --> 00:13:38,844
We made stools to sit on
in the washing area.

337
00:13:38,968 --> 00:13:40,230
- It seems to be going well.

338
00:13:40,357 --> 00:13:41,881
- Hm.

339
00:13:42,007 --> 00:13:43,226
- What is it?

340
00:13:43,353 --> 00:13:45,007
- I'm just now noticing this.

341
00:13:45,134 --> 00:13:48,050
Pulling water from the
river is fine and all,

342
00:13:48,173 --> 00:13:51,568
but is it okay to put
our wastewater

343
00:13:51,690 --> 00:13:53,605
back into the river
from our bath?

344
00:13:53,731 --> 00:13:55,428
- [Tia] If that's what
you're worried about,

345
00:13:55,555 --> 00:13:56,948
we can just use slimes.

346
00:13:57,075 --> 00:13:58,903
- Some slimes?
- Yeah.

347
00:13:59,029 --> 00:14:02,075
They eat waste and dead
organic matter and purify it.

348
00:14:02,199 --> 00:14:04,070
They're nature's
cleaning machines.

349
00:14:04,196 --> 00:14:06,328
- Aren't those
weak-looking monsters,

350
00:14:06,454 --> 00:14:08,369
that are actually really
dangerous and end up being

351
00:14:08,495 --> 00:14:10,715
the number one cause of
death in new adventurers?

352
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:12,667
[soul moaning]
[game beeping]

353
00:14:12,794 --> 00:14:14,404
- That's not how it is at all.

354
00:14:14,531 --> 00:14:16,794
I'll go catch some!

355
00:14:16,920 --> 00:14:18,922
All done.
[slime bouncing]

356
00:14:20,437 --> 00:14:23,353
- She grabbed them from
near the earlier village.

357
00:14:24,519 --> 00:14:25,694
[Kuro panting]

358
00:14:25,822 --> 00:14:27,345
Will you eat this?

359
00:14:28,730 --> 00:14:30,036
Okay, got it.

360
00:14:30,164 --> 00:14:32,906
[slimes plopping]

361
00:14:33,030 --> 00:14:35,206
I built a purification
pool for the slimes

362
00:14:35,332 --> 00:14:36,681
in the waste waterway.

363
00:14:36,809 --> 00:14:38,985
- If we put slimes
in the toilet,

364
00:14:39,110 --> 00:14:41,199
they'll clean everything
nasty in there for us.

365
00:14:41,325 --> 00:14:43,022
- I'm glad they'll do that,

366
00:14:43,149 --> 00:14:44,890
but I don't know if I have
the courage to do my business

367
00:14:45,016 --> 00:14:46,670
right above a slime's head.

368
00:14:46,797 --> 00:14:50,496
And just like that, the
wastewater problem was solved.

369
00:14:50,618 --> 00:14:52,795
Now I just need to
grab some firewood

370
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:54,704
and the bath will be
ready to go.

371
00:14:54,831 --> 00:14:56,180
Hm?

372
00:14:57,610 --> 00:14:59,003
A mushroom.

373
00:14:59,131 --> 00:15:00,785
I've actually been
too afraid to eat

374
00:15:00,912 --> 00:15:02,696
any of the mushrooms
in this forest,

375
00:15:02,823 --> 00:15:05,391
'cause I didn't know which
ones might be poisonous.

376
00:15:05,515 --> 00:15:07,343
- You made the right choice.

377
00:15:07,470 --> 00:15:10,038
Things like this are
really hard to tell apart.

378
00:15:10,163 --> 00:15:13,340
- They're pretty incredible
if you cook them thoroughly.

379
00:15:13,464 --> 00:15:16,597
- If you'd like me to, I'd be
happy to eliminate them.

380
00:15:16,722 --> 00:15:19,116
- [Hiraku] Huh? Is that
what we're talking about?

381
00:15:19,241 --> 00:15:21,722
The residents all had
different opinions.

382
00:15:21,847 --> 00:15:22,935
[light humming]

383
00:15:23,063 --> 00:15:24,456
In that case,

384
00:15:24,583 --> 00:15:26,368
Shiitake, shiitake, shimeji...
[hammer thumping]

385
00:15:26,494 --> 00:15:28,061
I went to hurry up and grow
all the mushrooms I knew.

386
00:15:28,189 --> 00:15:30,887
I'm not sure if this was
the right way to do it.

387
00:15:31,013 --> 00:15:32,405
Shiitake again.

388
00:15:32,533 --> 00:15:35,188
I completely forgot
about the bath.

389
00:15:35,704 --> 00:15:37,140
Ah.

390
00:15:37,268 --> 00:15:39,705
Now I'm going to teach you
how to use the bath.

391
00:15:39,831 --> 00:15:42,050
Take your clothes off
in the changing room.

392
00:15:42,177 --> 00:15:44,179
However, before you
get into the tub-

393
00:15:44,305 --> 00:15:45,480
- Ah?
- Ah?

394
00:15:45,609 --> 00:15:47,002
- [Hiraku] You first
need to rinse

395
00:15:47,129 --> 00:15:48,217
and lightly wash yourself off
in the washing area.

396
00:15:48,346 --> 00:15:49,695
- [Lea] Um, excuse me.

397
00:15:49,823 --> 00:15:51,302
- Hm?

398
00:15:51,431 --> 00:15:53,085
- It would be very helpful
if you could demonstrate.

399
00:15:53,211 --> 00:15:56,214
- You want me to show you?

400
00:15:56,340 --> 00:15:58,429
[cloth rustling]

401
00:15:58,555 --> 00:15:59,861
- Uh...

402
00:15:59,990 --> 00:16:01,556
First you get undressed,

403
00:16:01,684 --> 00:16:04,208
[water splashing]

404
00:16:04,335 --> 00:16:05,466
[elves humming]

405
00:16:05,595 --> 00:16:06,988
then you rinse yourself,

406
00:16:07,115 --> 00:16:08,551
then you wash yourself.

407
00:16:08,680 --> 00:16:12,075
Finally, get into
the bath and...

408
00:16:12,199 --> 00:16:15,333
Ah, it's the best.

409
00:16:15,458 --> 00:16:17,069
- [All] Ah.

410
00:16:17,196 --> 00:16:18,415
Oh?

411
00:16:18,543 --> 00:16:20,328
- I can really feel it.

412
00:16:20,455 --> 00:16:22,849
How long has it been
since I bathed like this?

413
00:16:22,976 --> 00:16:24,978
I wasn't allowed to
get into a bath

414
00:16:25,105 --> 00:16:26,759
while I was hospitalized.

415
00:16:26,888 --> 00:16:28,672
Huh? Zoned out.

416
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:30,410
So anyways, that's how
you enjoy it...

417
00:16:30,537 --> 00:16:31,756
- [All] Okay!

418
00:16:31,885 --> 00:16:34,583
[lively music beginning]
[elves giggling]

419
00:16:34,710 --> 00:16:36,537
- It's nice to be able to relax

420
00:16:36,666 --> 00:16:38,407
and wash ourselves like this.

421
00:16:38,534 --> 00:16:40,232
- Uh, sorry.

422
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:41,448
- Hm?
- Hm?

423
00:16:41,577 --> 00:16:42,752
- [Hiraku] No, it's just that...

424
00:16:42,881 --> 00:16:44,578
I'll get out first.

425
00:16:44,707 --> 00:16:46,099
You all can just take your time.

426
00:16:46,228 --> 00:16:47,359
- [Lu] Why is that?

427
00:16:47,489 --> 00:16:48,969
Can't we all just
bathe together?

428
00:16:49,097 --> 00:16:50,664
- [Tia] Yeah, She's right.

429
00:16:50,792 --> 00:16:53,316
This way we don't need to
heat up the water again.

430
00:16:53,443 --> 00:16:56,272
- Well, yeah,
you're right about that.

431
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:57,880
But still, I...

432
00:16:58,008 --> 00:16:59,531
[water bubbling]
I'm too embarrassed to relax

433
00:16:59,660 --> 00:17:01,444
with them all around
me right now.

434
00:17:01,573 --> 00:17:03,793
In the end, there wasn't
much time for me to relax

435
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:05,574
while in the bath.

436
00:17:05,703 --> 00:17:08,183
I should have built
a separate men's bath.

437
00:17:08,312 --> 00:17:10,444
- [Lu] Wouldn't that just be
a private bath for you?

438
00:17:10,572 --> 00:17:13,270
- [Tia] No fair, you can't
have a bath for just you.

439
00:17:13,399 --> 00:17:16,489
- [Hiraku] Is that what
you guys think?

440
00:17:16,615 --> 00:17:18,052
[wind rustling]
[footsteps approaching]

441
00:17:18,181 --> 00:17:19,095
Hm?

442
00:17:19,225 --> 00:17:20,705
[Hiraku laughing]

443
00:17:20,834 --> 00:17:22,357
Looks like it worked.

444
00:17:22,486 --> 00:17:24,357
Maybe I'll make a
mushroom hotpot tonight.

445
00:17:24,486 --> 00:17:26,357
[dog barking]
What?

446
00:17:26,487 --> 00:17:29,229
The dogs found five
new elves in the forest

447
00:17:29,356 --> 00:17:30,793
and brought them here.

448
00:17:30,922 --> 00:17:31,836
- I'm Lafa.

449
00:17:31,966 --> 00:17:32,793
- I'm Lassa.

450
00:17:32,923 --> 00:17:33,924
- I'm Lalasha.

451
00:17:34,054 --> 00:17:35,011
- I'm Lalu.

452
00:17:35,141 --> 00:17:36,098
- I'm Lami.

453
00:17:36,228 --> 00:17:37,359
?- [Hiraku] You're all "La?"

454
00:17:37,489 --> 00:17:39,883
- Oh, you mean our
names are "La."

455
00:17:40,012 --> 00:17:41,448
The reason our names are...

456
00:17:41,578 --> 00:17:43,449
- [Hiraku] You're all
related, right?

457
00:17:43,578 --> 00:17:44,361
- That's right.

458
00:17:44,492 --> 00:17:45,841
You already knew that?

459
00:17:45,971 --> 00:17:48,321
- [Hiraku] Do they all
want to live here too?

460
00:17:48,450 --> 00:17:49,974
- They do.

461
00:17:50,103 --> 00:17:52,149
They used to live in the
same village as all of us.

462
00:17:52,278 --> 00:17:53,584
- Since we left,

463
00:17:53,714 --> 00:17:55,280
we've been living our lives
as mere wanderers.

464
00:17:55,410 --> 00:17:57,673
It's been 200 years since
we've seen them.

465
00:17:57,803 --> 00:17:58,978
- 200?

466
00:17:59,108 --> 00:18:01,589
You must have had
a really rough time.

467
00:18:01,719 --> 00:18:02,937
It's fine by me.

468
00:18:03,067 --> 00:18:04,285
[Lafa gasping]

469
00:18:04,416 --> 00:18:06,331
If you'd like,
you can live with us.

470
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:08,288
- [All] Thank you very much.

471
00:18:08,418 --> 00:18:10,202
- All right, let's start
building you all

472
00:18:10,333 --> 00:18:11,726
a house to live in.

473
00:18:11,856 --> 00:18:13,597
I know. Why don't we
take this time

474
00:18:13,727 --> 00:18:15,859
to make some improvements
to your house?

475
00:18:15,990 --> 00:18:16,904
- Hm?

476
00:18:17,034 --> 00:18:18,862
Well, there are more people.

477
00:18:18,992 --> 00:18:21,081
I guess it's getting
kind of cramped.

478
00:18:21,211 --> 00:18:23,692
- We'll help you with
the work, so don't worry.

479
00:18:23,823 --> 00:18:26,129
- Oh, thank you.
That's helpful.

480
00:18:26,260 --> 00:18:29,872
- Okay, everyone, let's get
started on today's work.

481
00:18:30,003 --> 00:18:32,135
- [All] Okay.
[all giggling]

482
00:18:32,266 --> 00:18:34,529
And to ensure the
revival of our race,

483
00:18:34,659 --> 00:18:36,705
let's start making children.

484
00:18:36,836 --> 00:18:37,967
- [All] Yeah!

485
00:18:38,099 --> 00:18:39,753
[elves giggling]

486
00:18:39,883 --> 00:18:42,494
- I'm not sure how they
intended to make children,

487
00:18:42,625 --> 00:18:44,714
but it's nice to see
they're so optimistic.

488
00:18:44,846 --> 00:18:46,848
- Let's start now!
- What?

489
00:18:46,979 --> 00:18:48,851
- [Lea] It's time to
make houses.

490
00:18:48,981 --> 00:18:50,766
- [Hiraku] [stammering]
Yeah, let's go!

491
00:18:50,897 --> 00:18:52,072
Farming Life...

492
00:18:52,203 --> 00:18:53,247
- [Tia] in Another...

493
00:18:53,379 --> 00:18:54,684
- [Hiraku] World.

494
00:18:56,470 --> 00:18:58,472
- Let's start making children.

495
00:18:58,603 --> 00:18:59,430
- Yeah.
- Yeah!

496
00:18:59,562 --> 00:19:01,085
[elves giggling]

497
00:19:01,217 --> 00:19:02,827
- [Kuro] It appears
the number of females

498
00:19:02,959 --> 00:19:05,135
in my master's pack has
increased again.

499
00:19:05,266 --> 00:19:06,267
[Kuro growling]

500
00:19:06,399 --> 00:19:08,227
My name is Kuro.

501
00:19:08,358 --> 00:19:12,362
Before I met my master, I didn't
have a name to call my own.

502
00:19:12,496 --> 00:19:13,671
[nostalgic music beginning]

503
00:19:13,803 --> 00:19:15,587
Starting from the moment
I was born,

504
00:19:15,718 --> 00:19:18,504
I spent my whole life
in this forest alone.

505
00:19:18,636 --> 00:19:19,942
[footprints approaching]

506
00:19:20,075 --> 00:19:22,947
I never lost a single fight
to another male.

507
00:19:23,080 --> 00:19:24,995
I planned on living
my whole life

508
00:19:25,127 --> 00:19:28,914
doing whatever I pleased, and
hunting when I needed to eat.

509
00:19:29,048 --> 00:19:32,225
But one day, I met a female.

510
00:19:33,100 --> 00:19:34,536
[chime ringing]

511
00:19:34,668 --> 00:19:38,281
I didn't stand a chance
against her.

512
00:19:38,415 --> 00:19:40,287
After my complete loss
to that female,

513
00:19:40,420 --> 00:19:42,770
we began to travel together.

514
00:19:42,904 --> 00:19:46,560
Sometime after that,
her belly started to grow,

515
00:19:46,695 --> 00:19:50,438
and soon she gave birth
to our children.

516
00:19:50,574 --> 00:19:52,576
There are animals in this
forest who lead around

517
00:19:52,709 --> 00:19:54,407
packs of their little ones.

518
00:19:54,540 --> 00:19:56,934
When I thought about how that
would become my life one day,

519
00:19:57,069 --> 00:19:59,332
it didn't seem so bad.

520
00:19:59,465 --> 00:20:01,685
But then, our luck
took a turn for worse.

521
00:20:01,819 --> 00:20:03,212
[wolf whining]

522
00:20:03,346 --> 00:20:05,914
We ran into the one they
call the grappler bear,

523
00:20:06,048 --> 00:20:07,745
the king of this forest.

524
00:20:07,879 --> 00:20:10,795
I don't know if he decided
on a whim to spare us,

525
00:20:10,932 --> 00:20:14,239
or if he was just full,
but he didn't eat us.

526
00:20:14,376 --> 00:20:15,986
We were still gravely injured,

527
00:20:16,120 --> 00:20:19,427
and as a result,
we couldn't hunt for food.

528
00:20:19,565 --> 00:20:23,221
We'd become so weak that our
former prey had driven us away.

529
00:20:23,359 --> 00:20:26,580
We found ourselves at
the center of this forest,

530
00:20:26,717 --> 00:20:30,286
a place where even the grappler
bear doesn't dare to tread.

531
00:20:32,038 --> 00:20:33,431
[footsteps approaching]
[Hiraku humming]

532
00:20:33,565 --> 00:20:36,046
What we did find there
was a human male.

533
00:20:36,177 --> 00:20:37,787
- Hm?

534
00:20:37,917 --> 00:20:39,310
- [Kuro] I always thought that
people living in the forest

535
00:20:39,441 --> 00:20:40,703
kept themselves hidden,

536
00:20:40,833 --> 00:20:43,532
and never stayed in
one place for too long.

537
00:20:43,662 --> 00:20:46,491
How could someone
so obviously weak-looking

538
00:20:46,622 --> 00:20:48,841
survive here all by himself?

539
00:20:49,842 --> 00:20:51,235
It was that.

540
00:20:51,366 --> 00:20:54,108
I felt a limitless power
coming from that tool.

541
00:20:54,238 --> 00:20:56,849
We thought our lives
were over,

542
00:20:56,980 --> 00:20:59,287
and we'd already made
our peace with that.

543
00:20:59,417 --> 00:21:00,810
- Hm.

544
00:21:00,940 --> 00:21:02,116
[wolves chewing]

545
00:21:02,246 --> 00:21:04,161
- [Kuro] But he shared
his prey with us.

546
00:21:04,292 --> 00:21:05,641
He took care of us.

547
00:21:05,771 --> 00:21:06,859
[lighthearted music playing]

548
00:21:06,990 --> 00:21:09,253
This is the meat of a gate boar.

549
00:21:09,384 --> 00:21:12,561
I'm impressed that he was able
to hunt such a great beast.

550
00:21:14,519 --> 00:21:16,956
We don't have any desire
to fight him.

551
00:21:17,087 --> 00:21:19,046
The female and I have
decided that this male

552
00:21:19,176 --> 00:21:21,048
will be our master.

553
00:21:21,178 --> 00:21:25,139
Our master gave us names,
as well as a home to live in.

554
00:21:25,269 --> 00:21:27,010
The meat he cleans for us

555
00:21:27,141 --> 00:21:29,404
and the vegetables
he cooks are delicious.

556
00:21:29,534 --> 00:21:33,451
But the most delicious part
of an animal is the innards.

557
00:21:33,582 --> 00:21:35,671
Throwing that away
is a terrible waste.

558
00:21:35,801 --> 00:21:40,937
Before long, our children grew
up and our family got bigger.

559
00:21:41,068 --> 00:21:43,418
Our master also became
the leader

560
00:21:43,548 --> 00:21:45,724
of a large pack of his own.

561
00:21:45,855 --> 00:21:47,944
Looking at all the
females he leads,

562
00:21:48,075 --> 00:21:49,902
I can't help but think
that he must be more

563
00:21:50,033 --> 00:21:52,644
than just a weak human,
as I once thought he was.

564
00:21:52,775 --> 00:21:54,559
My only concern now

565
00:21:54,690 --> 00:21:58,085
is our master doesn't
seem to understand.

566
00:21:58,215 --> 00:22:00,913
He's unaware that we are
the terrifying monsters

567
00:22:01,044 --> 00:22:04,308
known as the inferno wolves.

568
00:22:04,439 --> 00:22:06,267
Well, I'm sure it'll be fine.

569
00:22:06,397 --> 00:22:07,616
[Kuro barking]

570
00:22:08,573 --> 00:22:10,358
Right now,

571
00:22:10,488 --> 00:22:14,797
I'm just thankful that my good
fortune led me here to him.

572
00:22:16,494 --> 00:22:19,845
["Feel the winds"
by Yui Hizuki plays]

573
00:23:46,541 --> 00:23:49,544
[rustic music playing]

